# Mother Ruxandra, archdruid of Yester Hill (docs/voice/ruxandra.md).
# summit: on the crown before the fight (approach). Every branch ends in the summit fight; how the party gets there
# decides who is in it (encounter summit_ritual's variants). fallen: after the fight, her fate.

~ summit
if flag.yester_sneaked and not flag.yester_struck_first
Narrator: The whole crown lies before you: druids swaying in a ring round the black tree, an old woman with both hands pressed to the effigy's chest, and nobody, nobody at all, looking your way.
* Strike now, while they chant. -> strike_first
* Step out and speak to her. -> speak
endif
-> speak

~ strike_first
set yester_struck_first
Narrator: You're across the ring before the first druid turns her head.
combat summit_ritual

~ speak
if not flag.ruxandra_met
set ruxandra_met
Narrator: The old woman straightens slowly from the effigy, wiping earth off her hands. Her face is kind. It's the kindest face you've seen in Barovia, and it doesn't change in the least when she looks at your weapons.
endif
if flag.kostin_fled and not flag.kostin_doubts
Ruxandra: Kostin told us you'd come. He was ashamed. I told him shame is only fear that has been taught manners.
elif flag.yester_heard
Ruxandra: We heard you in the gully, children. The hill hears everything. It's mostly ears.
else
Ruxandra: Guests. The hill gets so few guests. Mostly it gets offerings.
endif
Ruxandra: You've come for the bird-man's stone. It isn't his now. It's the heart of something better. Listen: you can almost hear it beating.
-> summit_menu

~ summit_menu
* We're taking the stone. Stand aside or don't. -> fight
* [Intimidation DC 17] Your lord isn't coming, and your circle can count. Run. -> rux_flee | rux_scorn
* [Religion DC 15] Your lord is a man in a castle. The land never needed his permission to grow. -> rux_religion | rux_scorn
* [if flag.elvir_story_heard and not flag.elvir_truth_known] A raven-man died on this hill last spring. -> rux_elvir
* [if not flag.ruxandra_asked_tree] What is that tree? -> rux_tree

~ rux_tree
set ruxandra_asked_tree
Ruxandra: Older than the castle. It grew from a stake pulled out of something that should have stayed dead, far away and long ago, and the mists carried the seed here, as they carry everything. It drinks. We give it to drink.
interject class:cleric: That isn't a tree. That's a grave that learned to stand up.
-> summit_menu

~ rux_elvir
set elvir_truth_known
if not flag.martikovs_reconciled
quest elvir_martikov truth_found
endif
Ruxandra: The black-eyed boy. Yes. He told his brother to fly, and the brother flew, and the boy laughed at us all the way up the hill. He stopped laughing, in the end. The tree is very thorough.
if name:wren_featherfoot
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Thank you. That's all we needed to hear.
else
interject tag:blunt: We heard. Every word of it.
endif
-> summit_menu

~ fight
Ruxandra: Then come and take it, children. Sing, all of you. Sing him awake.
combat summit_ritual

~ rux_scorn
Ruxandra: No. I don't think so. Sing, children. Louder.
combat summit_ritual

~ rux_flee
set yester_druids_fate = "fled"
Narrator: It isn't you they fear; it's the doubt, arriving all at once in a circle that never had any. One druid runs, then three. Ruxandra shrieks after them, gives you a look of perfectly polite hatred, and follows.
Ruxandra: The tree remembers faces!
Narrator: The chant stops half sung. In the silence, the effigy's chest cracks open anyway.
combat summit_ritual

~ rux_religion
set yester_circle_broken
Ruxandra: Clever. Unkind, but clever.
Narrator: Around the ring the humming falters. One druid lowers her hands, then another; they back away from the tree as if it had spoken their names, and go stumbling down the slope. Only Ruxandra stays, both hands on the effigy.
Ruxandra: Cowards. It doesn't matter. He has heart enough for all of us.
combat summit_ritual

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- After the fight

~ fallen
Narrator: Ruxandra lies among the roots of the black tree, breathing in small hitches. The roots have crept toward her while she lay there. She doesn't seem to mind.
Ruxandra: You broke him. You broke the heart. ...Well. The land will grow another. It always does.
-> fallen_menu

~ fallen_menu
* [if flag.elvir_story_heard and not flag.elvir_truth_known] Tell us about the raven-man you caged. -> fallen_elvir
* Go. Crawl off this hill and don't come back. -> spare
* End it. -> finish

~ fallen_elvir
set elvir_truth_known
if not flag.martikovs_reconciled
quest elvir_martikov truth_found
endif
Ruxandra: The bird-man's son? He sent his brother away. Ordered him off like a dog. He was proud of it; he told the tree so at the end. The tree didn't care. Trees don't.
-> fallen_menu

~ spare
set yester_druids_fate = "spared"
Ruxandra: Mercy. How like strangers. ...I'll go. The tree will call me back. It always calls us back.
Narrator: She gets up the way the very old do, in stages, and goes down the far side of the hill without once looking round.
approve liriel_dawnsong +2 wren_featherfoot +2: You let Ruxandra crawl off the hill alive
-> END

~ finish
set yester_druids_fate = "killed"
Narrator: It's quick. The roots that were reaching toward her draw back, as if they'd lost interest.
interject class:cleric: Go to whatever's waiting, mother. I hope it's kinder than your god.
approve thistle +1 liriel_dawnsong -1 wren_featherfoot -1: You finished Ruxandra where she lay
-> END
